*.swp

# archives — nothing in this repo should be a zip. public/images/products.zip
# (17 MB) and public/videos.zip (210 MB) were both dropped into public/ by
# accident, which meant they were being served to visitors. GitHub rejects any
# single file over 100 MB outright, so the videos zip could never have been
# pushed at all. Both are parked in source-assets/ locally.
*.zip

# unreferenced draft footage, ~187 MB across six files. These are Firefly
# generations kept for review; committing them would bloat every future clone
# for footage the site never loads. Delete them, or force-add with
# `git add -f` if a specific one is genuinely wanted.
public/videos/Firefly*.mp4

# delivery master for the hero, 32 MB at 25 Mbps. The site loads the 4.2 MB
# re-encode public/videos/himalayan-hero-ranges.mp4 (HeroVideo.tsx), which is
# tracked. Keeping the master out of git is the point of the re-encode — but
# keep the file locally, because it is what any future re-crop or re-grade
# has to start from. Regenerate the web copy with:
#   ffmpeg -i new_video.mp4 -c:v libx264 -preset slow -crf 27 -profile:v high \
#     -pix_fmt yuv420p -an -movflags +faststart himalayan-hero-ranges.mp4
public/videos/new_video.mp4
